Package: ofeIntegrateR
Title: Integrate Point-Source and High-Resolution Spatial Data in On-Farm Experiments
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Zhanglong", "Cao", , "jeromecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for designing cost-effective spatial sampling strategies
    and integrating sparse point-source measurements (e.g. soil cores, plant
    samples) with dense spatial covariates (e.g. EM38 surveys, yield maps) in
    on-farm experimentation (OFE) strip trials. Implements two integration
    strategies: a kriged-covariate approach (krige sparse point samples,
    then fit a spatial mixed model with the kriged surface as a fixed
    covariate) and a joint bivariate spatial model (point samples and
    high-resolution measurements modelled jointly via a shared spatial
    random effect). Developed for the AAGI-CU-RD-OFE GRDC project.
